{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":118,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"My son, pay attention to my wisdom. Turn your ear to my understanding,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":379},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":119,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"that you may maintain discretion, that your lips may preserve knowledge.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":382},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":120,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"For the lips of an adulteress drip honey. Her mouth is smoother than oil,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":385},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":121,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"but in the end she is as bitter as wormwood, and as sharp as a two-edged sword.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":388},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":122,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"Her feet go down to death. Her steps lead straight to Sheol.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":391},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":123,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"She gives no thought to the way of life. Her ways are crooked, and she doesn’t know it.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":394},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":124,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"Now therefore, my sons, listen to me. Don’t depart from the words of my mouth.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":398},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":125,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"Remove your way far from her. Don’t come near the door of her house,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":401},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":126,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"lest you give your honor to others, and your years to the cruel one;","is_omitted":0,"source_line":404},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":127,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"lest strangers feast on your wealth, and your labors enrich another man’s house.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":407},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":128,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"You will groan at your latter end, when your flesh and your body are consumed,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":410},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":129,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"and say, “How I have hated instruction, and my heart despised reproof.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":413},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":130,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"I haven’t obeyed the voice of my teachers, nor turned my ear to those who instructed me!","is_omitted":0,"source_line":416},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":131,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"I have come to the brink of utter ruin, among the gathered assembly.”","is_omitted":0,"source_line":419},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":132,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"Drink water out of your own cistern, running water out of your own well.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":423},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":133,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"Should your springs overflow in the streets, streams of water in the public squares?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":426},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":134,"verse_start":17,"verse_end":17,"verse_label":"17","text":"Let them be for yourself alone, not for strangers with you.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":429},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":135,"verse_start":18,"verse_end":18,"verse_label":"18","text":"Let your spring be blessed. Rejoice in the wife of your youth.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":432},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":136,"verse_start":19,"verse_end":19,"verse_label":"19","text":"A loving doe and a graceful deer— let her breasts satisfy you at all times. Be captivated always with her love.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":435},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":137,"verse_start":20,"verse_end":20,"verse_label":"20","text":"For why should you, my son, be captivated with an adulteress? Why embrace the bosom of another?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":439},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":138,"verse_start":21,"verse_end":21,"verse_label":"21","text":"For the ways of man are before the LORD’s eyes. He examines all his paths.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":442},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":139,"verse_start":22,"verse_end":22,"verse_label":"22","text":"The evil deeds of the wicked ensnare him. The cords of his sin hold him firmly.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":445},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:pro","chapter":5,"verse_ordinal":140,"verse_start":23,"verse_end":23,"verse_label":"23","text":"He will die for lack of instruction. In the greatness of his folly, he will go astray.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":448}]}